  "onbAlertsTitle": "Prayer alerts",
  "onbAlertsBody": "An Adhan alert at each prayer time, and a Jama’ah reminder before your mosque's Iqama. You can change every alert, its sound and its timing later in Settings.",
  "onbAlertsSwitch": "Adhan alert for the five prayers",
  "onbAlertsSwitchHint": "Your phone will ask to allow notifications.",
  "onbAlertsBattery": "Some phones stop alerts to save battery. If one doesn't arrive, set Jama’ah's battery use to Unrestricted in the phone's settings.",
  "onbTravelTitle": "Do you travel often?",
  "onbTravelBody": "Travel mode lets your prayer times follow you between cities and time zones, without changing your phone's clock. On a plane, it adds in-flight mode: prayer times and the Qibla aboard, from GPS, with no internet.",
  "onbTravelSwitch": "Turn on travel mode",
  "onbTravelHint": "You can switch it any time with the airplane at the top of the app.",
  "settingsShowIntro": "Show the introduction again",
  "inFlightHelp": "How it works",
  "inFlightHelpTitle": "In-flight mode",
  "inFlightHelpIntro": "Prayer times and the Qibla on a plane, with no internet and without changing your phone's clock.",
  "inFlightHelpStartTitle": "Starting it",
  "inFlightHelpStartBody": "Turn on travel mode with the airplane at the top of the app. On Today, tap “On a flight?”, then “Start GPS” and allow precise location. Sit by a window if you can: the phone's GPS works in airplane mode, but needs a view of the sky and can take a minute or two to find you.",
  "inFlightHelpTimesTitle": "The prayer times",
  "inFlightHelpTimesBody": "“Now” and “Next” are for where the aircraft is at this moment, shown on your phone's clock. Up high, the sun sets later and rises earlier than on the ground below, so Maghrib and sunrise follow the sun as you see it from the aircraft. Fajr and Isha follow your calculation method.",
  "inFlightHelpRouteTitle": "Along the route",
  "inFlightHelpRouteBody": "While the aircraft is moving, Jama’ah estimates when you will meet the next prayers if it keeps the same course and speed. The estimate updates with each GPS reading, so it gets better as the flight goes on. Flying east, prayers come sooner; flying west, the aircraft almost keeps pace with the sun, so sunset can stay hours away.",
  "inFlightHelpQiblaTitle": "The Qibla aboard",
  "inFlightHelpQiblaBody": "The phone's compass is not reliable inside an aircraft, so the arrow uses the direction the aircraft is flying, from GPS. It shows how far to the right or left of the nose the Qibla is. On the ground, or if you prefer, enter the heading shown on the seat-back map.",
  "inFlightHelpAlertsTitle": "Alerts in flight",
  "inFlightHelpAlertsBody": "While the aircraft is moving, your usual alerts for the place you left are paused, Jama’ah reminders too, and the next prayer along the route is alerted instead, marked as estimated. It uses that prayer's own Adhan settings. The pause ends by itself 90 minutes after the last GPS reading, or when you tap “End in-flight mode”. At home or at the gate nothing is paused.",
  "inFlightHelpTipsTitle": "Good to know",
  "inFlightHelpTipsBody": "Keep the in-flight screen open for the best updates; with the screen off for long, the phone may pause GPS. Nothing about where you are is sent anywhere. Questions about how to pray aboard, such as shortening or combining prayers, are for your scholar: Jama’ah gives the times and the direction only.",
  "notifInFlightBody": "It's time for {prayer}, estimated for the aircraft's route.",
  "@notifInFlightBody": {"placeholders": {"prayer": {"type": "String"}}},
  "inFlightAlongRoute": "Along this route: {prayer}, {countdown}",
